Descent
description: three dots — descendant-or-self along the containment spine
- >
  `...` fans out to the current node **and every contain-descendant** — descendant-or-self, pre-order.
  It walks the containment spine only: a ref edge is never crossed nor yielded by descent — reaching
  through refs is what explicit steps are for. The spine is acyclic and finite, so descent always
  terminates.
- !!<format: text/plain> |
  ...: !!<type: binary>          → every blob under here
  team: ...: !!<type: integer>   → :team:alice:age, :team:bob:age
  : ...: !!<type: object>        → :, :team, …  (the root itself too)
  thirty: ...                    → :thirty      (descent from a leaf is self)
